# MESSAGE: Segregation of duties — a principal holding both sides of an
# ip:conflictsWith / ip:SoDConflict pair without ip:sodExceptionReceipt is a
# refusal (dfcm:F5SegregationOfDuties). SoDConflict individuals must name both roles.
PREFIX ip: <https://ggen.dev/ontology/issue-platform-controls#>

SELECT DISTINCT ?subject ?problem WHERE {
  {
    ?subject a ip:SoDConflict .
    FILTER(
      NOT EXISTS { ?subject ip:leftRole ?l . ?l a ip:Role } ||
      NOT EXISTS { ?subject ip:rightRole ?r . ?r a ip:Role }
    )
    BIND("sod-conflict-missing-left-or-right-role" AS ?problem)
  } UNION {
    ?subject a ip:Principal ;
             ip:hasRole ?roleA ;
             ip:hasRole ?roleB .
    FILTER(?roleA != ?roleB)
    {
      ?roleA ip:conflictsWith ?roleB .
    } UNION {
      ?roleB ip:conflictsWith ?roleA .
    } UNION {
      ?c a ip:SoDConflict ;
         ip:leftRole ?roleA ;
         ip:rightRole ?roleB .
    } UNION {
      ?c a ip:SoDConflict ;
         ip:leftRole ?roleB ;
         ip:rightRole ?roleA .
    }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?subject ip:sodExceptionReceipt ?rx .
      FILTER(STRLEN(STR(?rx)) > 0)
    }
    BIND("principal-holds-conflicting-roles-without-exception-receipt" AS ?problem)
  }
}
ORDER BY ?subject ?problem
